First law of hacking: You'll find the exit at the entrance.

Terry Cline writes:
> 	Do you remimber where you came into that level at?  There will
> be a portal there that takes you back to the dungeon.  It's the ^ 
> shaped object.

Portals have the trap symbol because, to the game, they're a special
kind of level teleport trap.  Like any traps, they are not marked on
the map unless you find it, detect it, or activate it.

> A tip it to drop something upon entering a portal to mark the spot for
> eazy access.  The only other option is wandering around till you find it.

There are many ways to discover traps.  Some obvious ones:

- When you arrive on the Home level, take one step, then step back on
  the square you were on.  You'll activate the portal and go back to the
  Dungeons of Doom.  Portals don't disappear after one use, so you can
  return immediately.

- When you arrive on the Home level, 's'earch until you find the
  portal.  (Good wisdom exercise.)

- Wear or wield an item that conveys Searching, or play a class with
  intrinsic Searching.  Hang around the square until you find the
  portal.

- Cast the spell of detect unseen (or zap a wand of secret door
  detection) within range of the portal.

> 	Hold on, can't you Apply the orb to find features?  Try that
> and look for ^ but some are traps just ID them before stepping on them
> is all.

- Search for traps with a crystal ball.

